-- Operands of arithmetic that are not themselves arithmetic, as `l4 render`
-- reads them: a call, a rule's own sentence, an IF, a library date phrase.
-- Each pair has different values, and must read differently.
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT math

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`f2` a b MEANS a TIMES b

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg twice %a%
`twice` a MEANS a TIMES 2

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`call then minus` x MEANS `f2` 2 x MINUS 3

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minus in a call` x MEANS `f2` 2 (x MINUS 3)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sentence then minus` x MEANS `twice` x MINUS 3

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minus in a sentence` x MEANS `twice` (x MINUS 3)

GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN
      x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`if then minus` c x MEANS (IF c THEN 1 ELSE 10) MINUS x

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`year then minus` d MEANS (DATE_YEAR d) MINUS 1

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`months less one` d n MEANS `add months` d (n MINUS 1)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`times of minus` x MEANS 4 TIMES (x MINUS 2)

-- Pairs whose texts must differ, each needing more than precedence to read.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`call then minus then call` a b c d MEANS a MINUS `f2` b c MINUS d

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
      d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minus of a call of minus` a b c d MEANS a MINUS `f2` b (c MINUS d)

-- MODULO does not reassociate with TIMES or DIVIDED BY, so each pair below has
-- two values: 6 and 2, then 8 and 2, at 2, 7, 4; 2 and 0 at 12, 8, 2; 2 and 6
-- at 12, 2, 4.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`times of mod` a b c MEANS a TIMES (b MODULO c)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`mod of times` a b c MEANS (a TIMES b) MODULO c

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`mod then times` a b c MEANS (a MODULO b) TIMES c

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`mod of a product` a b c MEANS a MODULO (b TIMES c)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`mod then divided` a b c MEANS (a MODULO b) DIVIDED BY c

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`mod of a quotient` a b c MEANS a MODULO (b DIVIDED BY c)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`quotient then mod` a b c MEANS (a DIVIDED BY b) MODULO c

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`divided by a mod` a b c MEANS a DIVIDED BY (b MODULO c)

-- A call reads as f(x), which says where it ends, only when it has one input
-- and no sentence of its own. A rule that happens to share a name with a maths
-- function is bracketed like any other call: the name decides nothing.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      places IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`round` x places MEANS x TIMES places

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg the floor of %x%
`floor` x MEANS x TIMES 2

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`round then minus` a b c MEANS `round` a b MINUS c

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minus in a round` a b c MEANS `round` a (b MINUS c)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`floor then minus` x MEANS `floor` x MINUS 3

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minus in a floor` x MEANS `floor` (x MINUS 3)

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`exp then minus` x MEANS exp x MINUS 3

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minus in exp` x MEANS exp (x MINUS 3)

-- A mod beside + or −: tighter by the formula's rules, but a word, so a reader
-- can take "a − b mod c" to be (a − b) mod c.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`plus of mod` a b c MEANS a PLUS (b MODULO c)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minus of mod` a b c MEANS a MINUS (b MODULO c)

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`mod then minus` a b c MEANS (a MODULO b) MINUS c

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`mod of a difference` a b c MEANS (a MINUS b) MODULO c
